M32 random-route TP4 W2 NCU control/candidate comparison
Date: 2026-09-03
Both captures use profile_v4_flash_tp_local.py, one 256 MiB L2 clear before
the local pipeline, NCU cache-control=all, clock-control=none, and select only
the second route_gemm launch (W2).  Metric replay timings are diagnostic and
are not used as headline CUDA-Graph latencies.

Metric                              Control prefetch=0   Candidate prefetch=1
Duration (us)                       69.47                67.36
Executed instructions              24,803,501           25,017,941
Registers/thread                   48                   56
Dynamic shared KiB                 21.50                21.50
Achieved occupancy (%)             53.31                53.29
One or more eligible (%)           66.70                68.66
No eligible (%)                    33.30                31.34
Warp cycles / issued instruction   12.80                12.44
DRAM throughput (%)                47.80                49.39
Compute throughput (%)             64.20                66.47

Candidate W2 duration is 3.04% lower (1.031x speedup), despite executing 0.86%
more instructions.  Occupancy is unchanged.  The 1.96-point eligible-cycle
increase and 2.81% reduction in warp cycles per issued instruction support the
intended latency-hiding mechanism.

